   "daf": "33a",
   "sentenceId": 16,
   "he": "וְהֵן יוֹשְׁבוֹת עַל דָּם וְכוּ׳. תַּנְיָא, אָמַר רַבִּי מֵאִיר: אִם הֵן יוֹשְׁבוֹת עַל כׇּל דָּם וָדָם — תַּקָּנָה גְּדוֹלָה הִיא לָהֶן,",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches: «And» Samaritan men are considered men who engage in intercourse with menstruating women because «they observe» the seven-day menstrual period of impurity «for» each and every emission of «blood.» In this regard «it is taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Meir said: If» Samaritan women would begin «observing» a seven-day period of impurity «for each and every» emission of «blood, it» would be «a great remedy for them,» i.e., this practice would not lead to sin, as they would observe a seven-day period from each emission. But this is not their practice."
  }
 ],
